# The secrets the deploy screen asks for. Each one is described in package.json
# under "cloudflare".bindings, which is what the screen shows next to the field.
#
# This file is a list of names, not values. Nothing here is committed with a
# value in it, ever.
#
# ONE NAME, ON PURPOSE. The Deploy to Cloudflare screen treats every variable
# listed here as required: it will not deploy while one is empty. So a name
# added here for documentation's sake becomes a field the licensee must fill to
# get past their first screen, and the only way past it is to invent a value.
#
# That happened. ANTHROPIC_API_KEY was listed with a description saying it could
# wait, and the screen refused to continue without it - so it was filled with
# the console passphrase to get through. A licensee doing the same leaves
# believing they hold a model key, and finds out otherwise on the day they
# switch to the real model.
#
# Everything else is set after the deploy, when it is actually needed:
#
#   npx wrangler secret put ANTHROPIC_API_KEY     # step 4, turning on the model
#   npx wrangler secret put AMP_CHANNEL_THREADS_TOKEN
#   npx wrangler secret put AMP_CHANNEL_THREADS_USER_ID
#
# .env.local.sample lists them all, for running on your own machine.

# Required. Protects the approval console, which answers on the same address as
# the tracking redirect - so without it, anyone who knows the address can open
# the console.
AMP_CONSOLE_TOKEN=
